WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.220
1933. In the United States,

2
00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:06.700
about 25 per cent of
workers are unemployed.

3
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:11.100
Real output has fallen by
about a quarter since 1929.

4
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:14.380
Yet one theory says a slump cures itself.

5
00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.500
With so many people looking for work,

6
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.300
wages fall, costs fall,
and output recovers.

7
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.990
If that is true, why
do some economists say

8
00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:24.700
we should not wait?

9
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:27.980
In this mission, you'll watch
falling wages shift supply

10
00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:29.660
and close an output gap,

11
00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:31.160
step by step.

12
00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:34.090
Then you'll give two different
economies the same push

13
00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:36.980
in a graph lab, and compare what happens.

14
00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:41.400
Your mission: find out why some
economists would rather act than wait.
